{"@context":{"lean":"lean:","block":"block:","imports":{"@type":"@id"}},"@graph":[{"@id":"lean:module:UGB.BuchbergerPBW.ugb_pbw_corollary","@type":"LeanModule","name":"UGB.BuchbergerPBW.ugb_pbw_corollary","imports":["lean:module:Init","lean:module:UGB.GrobnerShirshov.NormalForms"],"declarations":1,"chunks":1},{"@id":"lean:UGB.BuchbergerPBW.ugb_pbw_corollary","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"UGB.BuchbergerPBW.ugb_pbw_corollary","kind":"theorem","line":73,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/unital-groebner-bases/lean/UGB/BuchbergerPBW/ugb_pbw_corollary.lean#L73-L112","doc":"**PBW corollary — `U_q(su(2))` instance.**\n\nWith `qs` the `q`-Serre data: every element reduces to a **unique** normal\nform under the `q`-Serre rewriting system. Existence is\n`normal_form_exists` (termination + monic rules, both discharged here);\nuniqueness is `normal_form_unique` against `qSerre_is_gs_basis`.\n\nThe former first conjunct — \"every PBW monomial is in normal form\" — is\n**gone, because it is false**; see the module docstring and\n`NormalForms.pbw_monomials_are_not_all_normal_forms`. What survives is a\nstatement about `ReducesToNF` over real `SU2Gen` types, and it no longer\ndepends on any refuted claim. ","formalizes":[{"@id":"block:cor:ugb-pbw","label":"cor:ugb-pbw","md":"unital-groebner-bases/buchberger-and-pbw/ugb-pbw-corollary.md"}],"signatureChunk":0}]}